&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;example-using-a-custom-video&#34;&gt;Example using a custom video
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;We provide an example of how to use our model to estimate scene layout starting from a RGB video with the newly released &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/PKU-VCL-3DV/SLAM3R&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;SLAM3R&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;EXAMPLE.md&#34; &gt;EXAMPLE.md&lt;/a&gt;. These steps work for MASt3R-SLAM, and other reconstruction methods as well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;spatiallm-testset&#34;&gt;SpatialLM Testset
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We provide a test set of 107 preprocessed point clouds, reconstructed from RGB videos using &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/rmurai0610/MASt3R-SLAM&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;MASt3R-SLAM&lt;/a&gt;. SpatialLM-Testset is quite challenging compared to prior clean RGBD scans datasets due to the noises and occlusions in the point clouds reconstructed from monocular RGB videos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dataset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Download&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;SpatialLM-Testset&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://huggingface.co/datasets/manycore-research/SpatialLM-TestSet&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;🤗 Datasets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;benchmark-results&#34;&gt;Benchmark Results
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;layout-estimation&#34;&gt;Layout Estimation
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Layout estimation focuses on predicting architectural elements, i.e., walls, doors, and windows, within an indoor scene. We evaluated this task on the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://structured3d-dataset.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Structured3D&lt;/a&gt; dataset. For &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/ywyue/RoomFormer&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;RoomFormer&lt;/a&gt;, we directly downloaded the model checkpoint. SceneScript and SpatialLM were first trained on our dataset, and further fine-tuned on Structured3D.&lt;/p&gt;
